   "qtype": "mcq",
   "section": "Section A",
   "stem": "Find out equivalent capacitance for the situation show in figure.",
   "correct_key": "B",
   "correct_value": null,
   "correct_keys": null,
   "solution": "Here,\n$C_1 = \\frac{2 \\times A\\varepsilon_0 K_1}{2d} = \\frac{A\\varepsilon_0 K_1}{d}$\n$C_2 = \\frac{A\\varepsilon_0 K_2}{d}$\n$C_3 = \\frac{A\\varepsilon_0 K_3}{2d}$\nNow $C_1$ and $C_2$ are in series\nSo, $\\frac{1}{C_1'} = \\frac{1}{C_1} + \\frac{1}{C_2}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{C_1'} = \\frac{d}{A\\varepsilon_0 K}\\left[\\frac{1}{K_1} + \\frac{1}{K_2}\\right] = \\frac{d(K_1 + K_2)}{A\\varepsilon_0 K_1K_2}$\n$\\Rightarrow C_1' = \\frac{A\\varepsilon_0 K_1K_2}{d(K_1 + K_2)}$\nNow $C_1'$ is parallel to $C_3$\n$\\Rightarrow C_{eq} = \\frac{A\\varepsilon_0}{d}\\left[\\frac{K_1K_2}{K_1 + K_2} + \\frac{K_3}{2}\\right]$\n$\\Rightarrow C_{eq} = \\frac{A\\varepsilon_0}{d}\\left[\\frac{2K_1K_2 + K_2K_3 + K_3K_1}{2(K_1 + K_2)}\\right]$",
   "marks_correct": 4,
   "marks_wrong": -1,
   "or_stem": null,
   "or_solution": null,
   "options": [
